  "question": "Given $$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix},\\quad B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\quad C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix},$$ calculate $(AB)C$ and $A(BC)$. Hence verify the associative property of matrix multiplication.",
  "answeroption": "C",
  "explanation": "<b>Product $AB$</b><br>$$AB=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$$<br><b>Evaluation of $(AB)C$</b><br>$$(AB)C=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 2 \\\\ 7 & 8\\end{bmatrix}$$<br><b>Product $BC$</b><br>$$BC=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$$<br><b>Evaluation of $A(BC)$</b><br>$$A(BC)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 2 \\\\ 7 & 8\\end{bmatrix}$$<br><b>Associative property</b><br>Thus, $(AB)C=A(BC)$.",
